<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Basic Statute of Oman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1996">1996</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Basic Law of Oman</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Basic Statute of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a> is the country's constitutional document, issued by royal decree of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qaboos-bin-said">Qaboos bin Said</a> in November 1996. It defines Oman as an Arab, Islamic and independent state ruled by a hereditary sultan, sets out rules of succession and basic rights, and provides for the Council of Oman, including the elected consultative council. It was revised in 2011 and 2021.</p></div>
